      longDescription: "Agricultural gypsum is calcium sulphate dihydrate (CaSO4\xB72H2O, CAS 10101-41-4), mined and ground to below 2 mm, with 85% minimum purity; pure gypsum carries 23.3% calcium and 18.6% sulphur, so the product delivers at least about 20% calcium and 16% sulphur. It is the standard amendment for reclaiming sodic and saline-sodic soils across Oman's irrigated regions, where saline groundwater raises exchangeable sodium, disperses clay and destroys soil structure and infiltration. Gypsum supplies soluble calcium that displaces sodium from the cation exchange complex, so the soil re-aggregates and water moves through it again. It is also a non-acidifying calcium and sulphur source for peanuts, alfalfa and forage crops. Global Chemicals LLC supplies it from stock in Muscat in 25 kg bags, 1,000 kg big bags and bulk.\n\nHow much to apply. The dose depends on the exchangeable sodium percentage and the cation exchange capacity, which only a soil test gives; a working rule is about 1.7 tonnes of pure gypsum (about 2 tonnes of this 85% product) per hectare for every milliequivalent of exchangeable sodium per 100 g of soil to be replaced in the top 15 cm, which is why field rates run from 2 to 10 t/ha. Gypsum dissolves slowly (roughly 2.5 g/L), so the fine grind matters: finer particles react faster. Reclamation only works if the displaced sodium is leached out, so spread the gypsum before an irrigation that drains below the root zone and plan follow-up leaching with the best-quality water available.\n\nGypsum can also be dissolved in irrigation water to raise its calcium and lower its sodium adsorption ratio before it reaches the soil, which protects infiltration on drip and sprinkler schemes fed from brackish wells. Because it does not change soil pH and does not burn foliage, it can be applied to standing date palm, vegetables and forage without a withdrawal period, and it can be blended with most fertilizers except those that react with calcium, such as phosphates.\n\nStore bags dry; the product is not hazardous and needs no special handling beyond dust control. Stock ships from our Muscat warehouse: same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar and Al Batinah, two to three days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road to the UAE (Dubai and Abu Dhabi three to five business days), Saudi Arabia (four to seven), Qatar, Kuwait and Bahrain with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the tonnage, bag size and delivery point.",
