      longDescription: "Laboratory acetone (propanone, CH3COCH3, CAS 67-64-1) is a clear, colourless, fast-evaporating solvent supplied by Global Chemicals LLC at 99.5% minimum purity to ACS reagent specification, water below 0.5%, with an HPLC/spectroscopy grade, in 500 mL, 2.5 L and 4 L bottles from stock in Muscat, each lot with a certificate of analysis and safety data sheet. It boils at 56 \xB0C, has a density of 0.79 g/mL and mixes with water and almost every organic solvent.\n\nWhat laboratories use it for. Rinsing and drying glassware after washing, because it carries water away and evaporates in minutes without residue; dissolving and extracting oils, fats, resins and many organic compounds; preparing samples for GC and other analyses; as a developing solvent or component in thin-layer chromatography; as a reaction solvent in synthesis; and cleaning instrument parts, syringes and cuvettes. Acetone absorbs strongly in the ultraviolet below about 330 nm, so it is a poor HPLC mobile phase for UV detection; the HPLC grade is bought for its low residue and particulate in sample preparation and cleaning, not as an eluent for low-UV work.\n\nMaterials and compatibility. Acetone dissolves or softens many plastics, including polystyrene, PVC, polycarbonate and acrylic, and attacks some rubbers and paints. Use glass, stainless steel, PTFE or polypropylene and HDPE containers and tubing, and check plastic labware before using it there. Wear butyl or laminate gloves; nitrile gives only brief splash protection.\n\nHandling and storage: acetone is highly flammable (UN 1090, Class 3) with a flash point of about \u221220 \xB0C, so its vapour can ignite at any room temperature. Keep bottles closed in a flammables cabinet away from heat, sparks and oxidisers, especially mixtures of nitric and sulphuric acid or hydrogen peroxide, with which it can react violently. Dispense in a fume hood or ventilated bench, earth metal containers for larger transfers, and wear safety glasses; the vapour irritates eyes and causes drowsiness at high concentration.\n\nThe laboratory chemicals supplier guide linked on this page lists the full solvent and reagent range. Delivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, two to three days to Nizwa, Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the grade, bottle size and quantity.",
