      longDescription: "Absolute ethanol (anhydrous ethyl alcohol, C2H5OH, CAS 64-17-5) is laboratory ethanol at 99.5\u201399.9% with water below 0.5%, supplied by Global Chemicals LLC from stock in Muscat in 500 mL, 1 L and 2.5 L bottles, with 5 L for larger users, in ACS reagent, molecular-biology (DNase- and RNase-free) and HPLC grades, each with a certificate of analysis and safety data sheet. State the grade and whether your permit covers undenatured spirit when ordering; denatured absolute ethanol is supplied where it does not. The industrial and 70% sanitiser grades are separate products.\n\nWhy the water content matters. Ordinary rectified spirit stops at the 95.6% azeotrope; absolute ethanol is dried past it with molecular sieves, and that last 4% of water is what the laboratory is paying to remove. Nucleic-acid work needs it: two to two-and-a-half volumes of cold absolute ethanol with salt precipitate DNA and RNA, and a 70% wash made from it removes the salt. Histology dehydrates tissue through a graded ethanol series ending in absolute before clearing and wax embedding. HPLC and spectroscopy need the HPLC grade for low UV absorbance and no particulate; NMR sample work and other water-sensitive preparations, plant and natural-product extraction, and the preparation of reference standards all need the anhydrous grade. GMP facilities use it for cleaning validation and equipment rinsing where a residue-free solvent is required.\n\nHandling and storage: absolute ethanol is highly flammable (UN 1170, Class 3) and hygroscopic. Keep bottles tightly closed, because the product absorbs water from the air and loses its anhydrous specification within days once opened; store them in a flammables cabinet away from oxidisers and heat, and dispense in a fume hood or ventilated bench with earthed metal containers for larger volumes. It is low in toxicity in use but dries skin; wear nitrile gloves and safety glasses. Molecular-biology grade should be aliquoted into small sterile bottles to keep the stock free of nucleases.\n\nThe laboratory chemicals supplier guide linked on this page lists the full reagent range, grades and documentation. Delivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, two to three days to Nizwa, Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the grade, bottle size and quantity.",
