      longDescription: "Ammonium chloride (NH4Cl, CAS 12125-02-9) is a white crystalline salt supplied by Global Chemicals LLC at 99.5% minimum purity, moisture below 0.5%, pH 4.5\u20136.0 in 10% solution and a solubility of 37 g per 100 mL of water at 20 \xB0C, from stock in Muscat in 25 kg and 50 kg bags and 1,000 kg big bags.\n\nIn the oilfield it is a clay stabiliser. Water-sensitive shales and clay-bearing sands swell and slough when they meet fresh water; the ammonium ion exchanges onto the clay surface much as potassium does, holding the clay in place. A 2\u20134% ammonium chloride brine is the usual non-damaging completion, workover and perforating fluid for such formations, and it is often preferred to potassium chloride where potassium would interfere with downstream analysis or formation-water compatibility. The brine is compatible with most formation waters and leaves no precipitate; a saturated solution reaches about 1.07 sg (9 lb/gal), which sets its upper density limit. It also serves as a packer fluid, a well-kill fluid and an additive in water-based drilling muds for wellbore stability.\n\nOutside drilling, ammonium chloride is the flux in soldering and hot-dip galvanising, where it cleans the metal surface and removes oxides at the moment of coating; a nitrogen source (about 26% N) in fertilizer blends for rice and other chloride-tolerant crops; a component of textile printing and dyeing baths; and the electrolyte of zinc-carbon dry cells. Laboratories use it in buffer solutions with ammonia.\n\nDissolving ammonium chloride cools the water noticeably, so make brine in batches and allow it to reach ambient temperature before measuring density. The solution is mildly acidic and corrosive to mild steel over time, so add a corrosion inhibitor for long-term packer duty. Keep bags closed and dry; the salt is hygroscopic and cakes in humid coastal air. A certificate of analysis and a GHS safety data sheet come with every lot. Delivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, to the interior fields by arrangement, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the quantity and pack size.",
