      longDescription: "Calcium bromide (CaBr2, CAS 7789-41-5) is the heavy clear brine of completion and workover work. Global Chemicals LLC supplies it as 52% liquid at about 1.70 sg (14.2 lb/gal) and as 95% anhydrous powder for building or topping up brine on location, in drums, 1,000 L IBCs, bulk and 25 kg bags from stock in Muscat, with delivery to the interior fields. Calcium bromide alone covers the density range above calcium chloride up to about 1.71 sg; blended with calcium chloride it fills the 1.40\u20131.84 sg range economically, and with zinc bromide it reaches the densities ultra-high-pressure wells need.\n\nWhy a clear brine. A completion, packer or kill fluid must balance reservoir pressure without carrying solids into the perforations, and calcium bromide does that with a solution: no barite, no filter cake, no plugged pores, and good visibility of returns during the job. It is stable to 200 \xB0C with the right inhibitors, compatible with most formation waters and completion hardware, and it suits solids-free reservoir drilling, horizontal and extended-reach completions, coiled-tubing and intervention work. Pick the density from the true vertical depth and bottom-hole pressure, then check the crystallisation temperature of that brine against the coldest point in the system, usually the surface pits on a winter night in the interior, and adjust the salt blend so nothing crystallises in the lines.\n\nPreparing and maintaining it: dissolve the powder slowly into water or into calcium chloride brine with agitation, because the heat of solution is large, and let it cool before measuring density; filter the brine to the completion's cleanliness specification; add a corrosion inhibitor and oxygen scavenger for long packer-fluid service; keep returns clean and the brine can be reconditioned and reused, which matters at its price. The oilfield chemicals guide linked on this page lists the companion brines and additives.\n\nHandling: calcium bromide brine is dense, mildly corrosive and irritating to skin and eyes; wear gloves, goggles and a face shield, use steel or HDPE equipment, and contain spills, because bromide is toxic to aquatic life and corrosive to concrete. Every delivery carries a certificate of analysis giving density, bromide and chloride content and pH, a technical data sheet with density and crystallisation tables, and a GHS safety data sheet. Global Chemicals LLC is JSRS-registered and ISO 9001:2015 certified.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, to the interior fields by arrangement, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the target density, volume and location.",
