      longDescription: "Tetrahydrothiophene (THT, thiolane, C4H8S, CAS 110-01-0) is the odorant that gives natural gas its warning smell. Global Chemicals LLC supplies it at 99.0% minimum purity by GC, 36.4% sulphur, density 1.00 g/cm\xB3, boiling point 121 \xB0C and flash point 13 \xB0C, in sealed 208 L steel drums under a nitrogen blanket, with a batch certificate of analysis, to gas-distribution companies, city-gas projects and industrial fuel-gas operators across Oman and the GCC.\n\nWhy THT. Natural gas has no smell, and regulations require it to be detectable by smell at a fraction of the lower flammability limit, typically one fifth. Odorants are either mercaptan blends or THT. THT is chosen for pipeline networks because it resists oxidation, is not lost on the pipe wall to the same degree as mercaptans, and therefore holds a consistent odour intensity along long distribution runs and at the far ends of new networks; its smell is distinctive and does not fade in the pipe. Typical dosing runs at 10\u201325 mg of THT per cubic metre of gas, set by the regulator's detectability requirement and confirmed by sniff tests or a THT analyser at the network extremities. It is injected by a dosing skid proportional to the gas flow, or by a wick or bypass odoriser on small systems; the oilfield chemicals guide linked on this page covers related products.\n\nOther uses: odorising fuel gas and process gas for leak detection in industrial plants, biogas and syngas before grid injection, and LPG where the specification calls for THT rather than ethyl mercaptan.\n\nHandling: THT is a flammable liquid (UN 2412, Class 3) with an intense, penetrating odour; the smallest spill or vapour release triggers gas-leak reports across a neighbourhood. Keep drums sealed and nitrogen-blanketed until use, transfer with closed, earthed systems into the odoriser tank, store in a ventilated, shaded, bunded area away from ignition sources, and keep a sodium hypochlorite solution ready to oxidise and neutralise spills and contaminated PPE. Wear nitrile gloves, goggles and, for open handling, respiratory protection. Our technical team supplies dosing-skid compatibility information and the GHS safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is scheduled to gas-distribution stores and plants across Oman and by road to the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the number of drums and the delivery point.",
