      longDescription: "LABSA (linear alkylbenzene sulphonic acid, CAS 27176-87-0) is the raw material behind most liquid detergents. Global Chemicals LLC supplies the 96% grade from stock in Muscat in 200 kg HDPE drums and 1,000 kg IBCs to detergent manufacturers, cleaning-product formulators and industrial blenders across Oman and the GCC: a dark brown, viscous liquid with 96% minimum active matter, 0.5\u20132.0% free sulphuric acid, 2.0\u20134.0% unsulphonated material, Klett colour 40\u201360, specific gravity 1.05\u20131.06 and a flash point above 100 \xB0C.\n\nHow it is used. LABSA is an acid and is never used as such in a product; it is neutralised to sodium linear alkylbenzene sulphonate (SLAS or LAS), the anionic surfactant that does the cleaning and foaming. Neutralising 1 kg of LABSA takes about 125 g of sodium hydroxide, which is roughly 250 g of 50% caustic solution, to reach pH 7\u20138; add the acid slowly to the water and caustic with good stirring, because the reaction gives off heat, and finish the pH with a little acid or caustic. The resulting paste or solution is then built into the product: dish-wash liquids at 10\u201320% LAS with SLES and a foam booster, liquid laundry detergents, all-purpose and floor cleaners, car shampoos, toilet-bowl cleaners and industrial degreasers. Soda ash or triethanolamine can replace caustic where the formulation calls for them. Outside cleaning, LAS is an emulsifier in agrochemical formulations and a wetting agent in textile and leather processing.\n\nWhy LABSA: it is the lowest-cost surfactant per unit of cleaning, it is readily biodegradable in its linear form, it tolerates hard water when built with a chelant, and it blends with every common co-surfactant. The FAQs on this page give the standard ratios.\n\nHandling: LABSA is a strong acid that burns skin and eyes and attacks mild steel; store it in HDPE, stainless or lined tanks, keep drums closed and out of the sun to limit colour darkening, and wear gloves, goggles and a face shield. It is not flammable. Every delivery carries a certificate of analysis giving active matter, free acid, unsulphonated matter and colour, a technical data sheet, formulation guidance and a GHS safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road to the UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait and Bahrain with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the number of drums or IBCs and monthly volume.",
