          question: "What is industrial kerosene used for in Oman and how does it differ from aviation fuel?",
          answer: "Industrial kerosene (CAS 8008-20-6) is a petroleum distillate fraction with a boiling range of 150\u2013300\xB0C used as a fuel, solvent, and process chemical. In Oman, industrial kerosene applications include: agricultural and marine engine fuel for fishing boats and small vessels in Oman's coastal governorates; heating fuel for industrial ovens, dryers, and process heaters where natural gas is unavailable; cutting fluid and thread-cutting oil in metalworking (kerosene's low viscosity and flash point above 38\xB0C make it safe for light machining and tapping of non-ferrous metals); carrier and diluent in paints, wood preservatives, and agricultural crop sprays; and mosquito and pest control applications. Industrial (commercial) kerosene differs from aviation turbine fuel (Jet-A1) in its more variable specification \u2014 Jet-A1 has tighter controls on freeze point, flash point, acidity, and contaminant levels to meet ASTM D1655 requirements for aircraft safety. Industrial kerosene does not meet Jet-A1 specification and must not be used as aircraft fuel. Global Chemicals LLC supplies industrial kerosene in drums and IBC for Oman."
