      longDescription: "Chlorine powder for pools is calcium hypochlorite (CAS 7778-54-3) milled to a fine powder, with 65\u201370% available chlorine, pH 11\u201312 in solution and no cyanuric acid stabiliser. Global Chemicals LLC supplies it from stock in Muscat in 500 g, 1 kg, 5 kg, 25 kg and 50 kg packs to pool-maintenance companies, hotels, villa compounds and residential pool owners across Oman. It is the same chemistry as our calcium hypochlorite granules; the powder dissolves fastest and is dosed by weight, while the granules suit users who want less dust and a slower release.\n\nDosing by weight. With a 65% product, 15 g per 10,000 litres raises free chlorine by 1 mg/L, so the shock dose of 150\u2013300 g per 10,000 litres gives a 10\u201320 mg/L rise; weigh the dose from the pool volume and the chlorine reading rather than guessing. Pre-dissolve the powder in a clean plastic bucket of pool water, stir, let any residue settle, and pour the clear solution around the pool in the evening with the pump running so sunlight does not burn off the chlorine before it works. Never pour powder straight into a skimmer or a feeder that has held TCCA, and never broadcast it onto a liner or a dark surface, which it bleaches.\n\nWhat it is for: the weekly or twice-weekly shock programme of hotel and compound pools, breakpoint chlorination to destroy chloramines (dose at least ten times the combined-chlorine reading), rapid killing of green algae, clearing cloudy water, super-chlorination after parties, rain or heavy use, opening and closing pools, and emergency disinfection of tanks and lines. Because it carries no stabiliser it does not raise cyanuric acid, which stabilised tablets do; because it carries calcium, it raises hardness a little with each dose, which liquid chlorine does not.\n\nHandling and storage: calcium hypochlorite is an oxidiser (Class 5.1; UN 2880 for hydrated or UN 1748 for dry grades, or corrosive UN 3487/UN 3485, as given in section 14 of the SDS) that reacts violently with acids, TCCA, ammonia, fuels and organic matter, and the fine powder is an eye and respiratory irritant. Store it sealed, cool, dry and apart from every other chemical, add product to water and never water to product, and wear gloves, goggles and a dust mask. Every pack carries a GHS safety data sheet and certificate of analysis giving available chlorine.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the pack size and monthly quantity.",
