      longDescription: "Liquid aluminium sulphate (liquid alum, Al2(SO4)3 solution, CAS 10043-01-3) is a clear to light-yellow coagulant solution at 8\u20139% Al2O3, specific gravity 1.25\u20131.35 and pH 3.0\u20134.0 in 1% solution, supplied by Global Chemicals LLC in 1,000 L IBCs and bulk tanker from stock in Muscat, with jar-test support. The solid (alum powder or kibbled) is the same chemical for users who prefer to dissolve on site.\n\nWhat it does. Alum neutralises the negative charge on suspended particles and colour and forms aluminium hydroxide floc that sweeps them out of the water, so it is used to clarify drinking water, industrial process water and effluent, and to precipitate phosphorus in sewage treatment. It works best between about pH 5.5 and 7.5 and consumes alkalinity as it reacts, roughly 0.5 mg/L of alkalinity as CaCO3 for each mg/L of commercial alum (as the 14-hydrate), so soft or low-alkalinity waters often need lime or soda ash dosed alongside it. Doses run from a few to several tens of mg/L, set by jar test on the actual water. For a comparison with poly aluminium chloride, which forms floc faster over a wider pH range and consumes less alkalinity, see the PAC supplier guide; alum remains the economical choice for many plants with stable, well-buffered raw water.\n\nOther uses: paper sizing with rosin and pH control in paper mills; textile and dye-house effluent colour removal; and sludge conditioning.\n\nDosing and handling: liquid alum is acidic and corrosive to mild steel and concrete, so store it in polyethylene, FRP or rubber-lined tanks and dose with PVC or PE pipework and diaphragm or peristaltic pumps, neat or diluted just before the dosing point. It does not freeze in Oman's climate and keeps for months in closed tanks; wear gloves and goggles. Every delivery carries a certificate of analysis giving Al2O3, specific gravity and free acid or basicity, and a GHS safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, two to three days to Salalah and Duqm, by scheduled tanker to treatment plants, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the monthly volume and delivery point.",
