      longDescription: "Hydrated lime (calcium hydroxide, Ca(OH)2, CAS 1305-62-0) is slaked lime as a fine white powder, supplied by Global Chemicals LLC in technical grade at 90\u201396% calcium hydroxide, 68\u201374% available calcium oxide and pH 12.4 in a 1% suspension, in 25 kg and 50 kg bags and bulk from stock in Muscat. It is the alkali most water plants, contractors and industrial users reach for when they want the neutralising power of lime without the heat and handling of quicklime; the quicklime page covers the unslaked form.\n\nIn water treatment it is dosed as a 5\u201310% milk-of-lime slurry. Desalination and municipal plants across Oman use it with carbon dioxide to remineralise permeate, raising pH and adding the calcium and alkalinity that stop corrosive water attacking the distribution network. Lime softening precipitates carbonate hardness; at pH 10\u201311 and above it precipitates phosphate from sewage effluent, and at pH 9\u201311 heavy metals from mining and metal-finishing wastewater; at pH 12 held for two hours it stabilises sewage sludge; and it neutralises acidic effluent cheaply and without the overshoot of caustic. Flue-gas desulphurisation uses it to capture sulphur dioxide. The FAQs on this page cover dosing practice.\n\nIn construction, hydrated lime is the binder of lime mortars, plasters and renders, improves the workability and water retention of cement mortars, and at 2\u20135% by weight stabilises clay subgrades on the interior road projects, drying wet soil and raising its bearing strength within hours. Sugar refineries use it to purify juice, and tanneries, water-based paint and food-grade users each take their own grades.\n\nHandling and storage: hydrated lime is strongly alkaline and the dust burns eyes and irritates skin and airways, so wear gloves, goggles and a dust mask and mix slurries in a ventilated area. It absorbs carbon dioxide from the air and turns slowly back into calcium carbonate, losing strength, so keep bags closed, dry and off the floor and use older stock first. Every lot carries a certificate of analysis giving calcium hydroxide content, available lime, fineness and moisture, plus a GHS safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, two to three days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the bag size, tonnage and delivery point.",
