      longDescription: "Poly aluminium chloride liquid (PAC, CAS 1327-41-9) is a pre-polymerised aluminium coagulant supplied by Global Chemicals LLC at 10\u201311% Al2O3 with 40\u201390% basicity, pH 3.5\u20135.0 in 1% solution, as a clear to light-yellow liquid in 1,000 L IBCs and bulk tanker from stock in Muscat, with jar-test support and dosage optimisation from our technical team. It is widely used in Oman's water plants, and the full grade comparison, specification table and FAQs are on the poly aluminium chloride supplier guide linked on this page; the powder grade is listed separately.\n\nWhy PAC rather than alum. The aluminium in PAC is already polymerised and carries a high positive charge, so it neutralises the charge on turbidity and colour particles and builds floc faster, at lower dose, over a wider pH range (5.0\u20139.0) and in colder or low-turbidity water than aluminium sulphate. It consumes less alkalinity, so plants need less lime or caustic to hold pH; it leaves less residual aluminium in the treated water; and it produces less, denser sludge. Typical doses run from a few milligrams per litre on clean well water to tens of milligrams per litre on turbid surface water or wastewater, and the jar test sets the figure for each water.\n\nWhere it is used: clarification in municipal and industrial drinking-water plants, primary and tertiary treatment of sewage and industrial effluent, removal of colour and suspended solids from textile and paper wastewater, phosphorus removal, swimming-pool clarification, and pre-treatment ahead of reverse-osmosis desalination, where the dose must be set by jar test and the clarified water filtered so residual aluminium does not reach the membranes.\n\nHandling and storage: PAC liquid is acidic and corrosive to mild steel; store it in polyethylene, FRP or rubber-lined tanks and dose it with PVC or PE lines and diaphragm pumps, undiluted or diluted just before the dosing point. Keep tanks shaded and closed; the product is stable for six to twelve months and does not freeze in Oman's climate. Wear gloves and goggles. Every delivery carries a certificate of analysis giving Al2O3, basicity, pH and density, plus a GHS safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, two to three days to Salalah and Duqm, by scheduled tanker to treatment plants in every governorate, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the Al2O3 grade, monthly volume and delivery point.",
