      longDescription: "Sodium hexametaphosphate (SHMP, Graham's salt, a glassy sodium polyphosphate written (NaPO3)n, CAS 68915-31-1) is supplied by Global Chemicals LLC as white powder or granules with at least 68% P2O5 and pH 5.8\u20137.3 in 1% solution, in technical grade and food grade (E452(i)), in 25 kg bags from stock in Muscat.\n\nWhat it does. SHMP sequesters calcium, magnesium and iron into soluble complexes and, at very low doses, distorts the growth of calcium carbonate crystals so scale does not form; this threshold effect works at roughly 1\u20135 mg/L. It is therefore used to prevent scale in cooling water, evaporative coolers and some boiler-feed and process-water systems, to keep iron and manganese in solution so they do not stain, as a dispersant for clay and pigment slurries, and as a sequestrant and builder in detergents and cleaners. Polyphosphates slowly revert to orthophosphate in water, faster in heat and at low pH, so SHMP solutions should be made up fresh and its scale control weakens at higher temperatures and fails in boilers. For corrosion control of lead and copper in drinking-water networks, utilities rely mainly on orthophosphate and pH control, so SHMP is not a lead-control treatment on its own.\n\nFood uses: as E452(i) it is a sequestrant, emulsifying salt and water-binding agent in processed cheese, processed meat and poultry, seafood such as frozen prawns, and some dairy and beverage products, within the phosphate limits of food law. The food grade carries its own certificate and specification.\n\nOther industrial uses: a deflocculant in ceramics and clay processing, a dispersant in drilling mud and mineral processing, and a component of metal-cleaning and surface-treatment baths.\n\nHandling and storage: SHMP is low in hazard; the dust irritates eyes, so wear goggles and a dust mask when tipping bags. It is hygroscopic and the glassy form becomes sticky in humid air, so keep bags closed and dry. Every lot carries a certificate of analysis giving P2O5 and pH, and a safety data sheet.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road to the UAE, Saudi Arabia and the rest of the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the grade and quantity.",
