      longDescription: "Sodium metabisulphite (SMBS, sodium pyrosulphite, Na2S2O5, CAS 7681-57-4) is a white crystalline powder supplied by Global Chemicals LLC at 96% minimum purity, about 65% available SO2 (pure SMBS carries 67.4%) and pH 4.0\u20135.5 in 1% solution, in technical grade and food grade (E223), in 25 kg bags from stock in Muscat. In water it forms sodium bisulphite, about 1.1 kg of NaHSO3 per kg, which is why it is the solid form of the dechlorination chemical.\n\nDechlorination before reverse osmosis. Polyamide thin-film membranes are oxidised and permanently damaged by free chlorine, so desalination and industrial RO plants dose SMBS solution ahead of the membranes after chlorinating the intake against biofouling. The theoretical need is about 1.34 mg of SMBS per mg of free chlorine; plants dose more to keep a margin and confirm with an ORP or residual-chlorine reading downstream. Make up the dosing solution at around 5\u201310% in clean water and use it within a few days, because it oxidises in the tank and loses strength. The dosing calculator on this site has a dechlorination tool for sizing the feed.\n\nFood, beverage and other uses: as E223 it is an antioxidant and preservative in dried fruit, juices, wine and some processed foods, and a sanitising agent for brewing and winemaking equipment; products containing more than 10 mg/kg of sulphite as SO2 must declare it as an allergen. In industry it is an oxygen scavenger in low-pressure boiler water, a reducing agent for chromium in effluent and for dechlorinating discharges, an antichlor in textile and pulp bleaching, a photographic chemical, and a reagent in gold processing.\n\nHandling and storage: SMBS releases sulphur dioxide gas on contact with acids and slowly in moist air; the gas irritates the airways and can trigger asthma. It is harmful if swallowed and causes serious eye damage, so wear goggles, gloves and a dust mask and mix solutions in ventilated areas. Keep bags closed, dry and cool, away from acids and oxidisers. Every lot carries a certificate of analysis giving assay and SO2 content, and a GHS safety data sheet; the food grade carries food-safety documentation.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the grade and quantity.",
