      longDescription: "Sodium sulphite (Na2SO3, CAS 7757-83-7) is a white crystalline powder supplied by Global Chemicals LLC at 96% minimum purity, pH 9\u201310 in 1% solution, in technical grade and food grade (E221), in 25 kg bags from stock in Muscat.\n\nBoiler oxygen scavenging. Dissolved oxygen in boiler feedwater pits steel tubes, drums and condensate lines. Sodium sulphite reacts with it to form sodium sulphate: the theoretical requirement is 7.9 mg of sodium sulphite per mg of oxygen, and in practice about 10 mg/mg is fed after mechanical deaeration, plus enough to hold a residual of typically 20\u201340 mg/L as sulphite in low-pressure boiler water. It is the economical scavenger for low- and medium-pressure boilers, generally below about 40 bar; above that it decomposes into corrosive sulphur compounds and adds dissolved solids, so hydrazine substitutes or other volatile scavengers are used instead. The reaction is slow in cold water, which is why catalysed grades are used where feedwater is not heated; feed it continuously into the storage section of the deaerator or feed tank, away from air contact. Food plants, laundries, hospitals and hotels running steam boilers across Oman use it this way.\n\nOther uses: a dechlorinating agent for water and effluent; an antioxidant and preservative (E221) in foods and dried fruit, which must be declared as a sulphite allergen above 10 mg/kg as SO2; a reducing agent in textile processing and in pulp bleaching; and a component of photographic developers.\n\nHandling and storage: sodium sulphite oxidises slowly to sulphate in moist air, so keep bags closed, dry and cool and make up dosing solutions fresh. It releases sulphur dioxide on contact with acids, which irritates the airways; store it away from acids and oxidisers, and wear gloves, goggles and a dust mask when handling. Every lot carries a certificate of analysis giving assay and a safety data sheet, and our water-treatment team supplies dosing calculations for boilers.\n\nDelivery is same day within Muscat, next day to Sohar, 2\u20133 days to Salalah and Duqm, and by road across the GCC with a certificate of origin. Request a quote with the grade, quantity and boiler details.",
